all, hydration is a multifaceted process that influences health outcomes, exercise performance, and the management of various medical conditions, highlighting the importance of adequate fluid intake across different contexts.\",18\r\n3343,EJERCICIO FÍSICO,\"\"\"EJERCICIO FÍSICO\"\" refers to physical activity that encompasses any bodily movement aimed at improving physical fitness and overall health. It is characterized by being voluntary, planned, structured, and repetitive, with the goal of enhancing bodily function. Ejercicio físico is particularly significant for various populations, including individuals with diabetes, as it can impact blood sugar levels and necessitates careful management. It is also recommended for patients with obesity to improve their health and well-being.\n\nIn the context of elderly individuals, physical exercise is advised to be combined with amino acid supplementation to promote better muscle health. Research has shown that physical exercise interventions can enhance muscle strength and physical performance, especially in frail elderly individuals. Regular physical activity is crucial for maintaining bone health, facilitating the synthesis of vitamin D, and preventing the loss of lean body mass in older adults. Additionally, it is beneficial for individuals with hypertension, as it can help lower blood pressure.\n\nOverall, ejercicio físico is emphasized as an essential component of a healthy lifestyle, working in conjunction with proper nutrition and hydration to optimize health outcomes across different populations.\",24\r\n27,DESHIDRATACIÓN,\"\"\"DESHIDRATACIÓN\"\" refers to dehydration, a condition that occurs when the body loses more fluids than it takes in, which can significantly affect overall health and performance. It is a common consequence of various medical conditions, including watery diarrhea, particularly in patients with a congenital deficit of saccharase-isomaltase. Dehydration can also arise from oropharyngeal dysphagia, which complicates the clinical situation for affected patients, as well as from difficulties in swallowing and eating, especially in individuals with head and neck tumors. Additionally, patients undergoing enteral nutrition may experience dehydration due to negative fluid balance, leading to symptoms such as dryness of the skin and mucous membranes. Proper hydration is crucial, particularly during exercise, to prevent dehydration and its associated health risks. Overall, dehydration is a serious condition that can lead to significant health issues if not properly managed.\",9\r\n12116,SRO,\"SRO refers to Oral Rehydration Solutions, which are used to prevent dehydration caused by diarrhea.\",2\r\n14365,EJERCICIO DE ULTRARESISTENCIA,\"El ejercicio de ultrarresistencia se refiere a actividades físicas que duran más de 2,5-3 horas, donde se requiere una ingesta elevada de carbohidratos para mantener el rendimiento.\",1\r\n14386,GASTO DE GLUCÓGENO MUSCULAR,\"Muscle glycogen expenditure refers to the use of stored carbohydrates in muscles during physical activity, which can be influenced by hydration and carbohydrate intake.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3490,PACIENTE,HIDRATACIÓN,\"The hydration of the patient is a crucial aspect of their nutritional health. It is particularly vital for patients receiving enteral nutrition, as it ensures their overall well-being and health. Proper hydration is essential for all patients, as it helps prevent complications such as constipation. Therefore, maintaining adequate hydration is a key component of patient care and nutrition management.\",564\r\n4966,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,EJERCICIO FÍSICO,Physical activity is encouraged to enhance the health of patients receiving parenteral nutrition.,462\r\n4001,HIDRATACIÓN,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"HIDRATACIÓN and NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL are closely related concepts in the context of patient care, particularly for those who are un